Corporate Enforcer
Core Corporate Enforcer Class Features
1. Combat Augment Protocol (Level 1)
You calibrate your neural interface and physical sub-dermal augments for a specific combat doctrine:

Smart Link Targeting
You gain a +2 bonus to attack rolls made with ranged smart-weapons and firearms.

Sub Dermal Plating
You gain a +1 bonus to AC while wearing armor or sub-dermal weave.

Monomolecular Edge Tuning
When wielding a one-handed melee weapon in one hand and no other weapons, you gain a +2 bonus to damage rolls.

Hydraulic Torque Drive
When you roll a 1 or 2 on a damage die for an attack with a two-handed weapon, you can reroll the die and must use the new roll.

Hard Light Aegis Intercept
When a target within 5 feet of you is attacked, you can use your reaction to project a hard-light barrier, imposing disadvantage on the attack roll (requires a shield or cyber-shield).

Dual Rotor Actuators
When you engage in two-weapon fighting, you can add your ability modifier to the damage of the second attack.

2. Nanite Repair Injection (Level 1)
You activate a sub-dermal auto-injector or trigger a nanite repair swarm that instantly cauterizes wounds, seals flesh, and numbs trauma.

Mechanics
On your turn, you can use a bonus action to regain Hit Points equal to 1d10 + your Fighter level. (1/Short or Long Rest).

3. Synaptic Overclock (Level 2)
You temporarily override your neural safety governors or trigger a heavy combat-stim dump, allowing your body to move at near-light reaction speeds.

Mechanics
On your turn, you can take one additional action on top of your regular action and possible bonus action. (1/Short or Long Rest; 2 uses at Level 17).

4. Combat Specialization (Level 3)
You select your operational role in Neo-Tokyo's shadow economy—whether as a street samurai, corporate field officer, or spirit-bound ward-knight.

5. Rapid Fire Protocol (Level 5)
High-frequency weapon swings, sub-dermal recoil dampeners, and automated target cycling allow you to strike multiple targets in milliseconds.

Mechanics
You can attack twice (Level 5), three times (Level 11), and four times (Level 20) whenever you take the Attack action on your turn.

6. Neural Hardening (Level 9)
You purge Black ICE neural feedback, override bioweapons, or push through physical shock through sheer grit and hardened firewall firmware. :::

Mechanics
You can reroll a saving throw that you fail, but you must use the new roll. (1/Long Rest at Level 9; 2 at Level 13; 3 at Level 17).

